    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d299-a1">

                <pb facs="0343" n="267" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg267"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Hartman to the Minister of Foreign Affairs
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 210</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Quito</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-10-03">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 3, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: By direction of my Government, I
                    have the honor to inform your excellency that while it would be greatly
                    gratified at the securing of a loan by your excellency’s Government and the
                    payment of the obligations of Ecuador to the Guayaquil &amp; Quito Railway
                    Company from the proceeds thereof, it nevertheless entertains the belief that
                    present conditions appear to indicate that no definite arrangement for such a
                    loan is to be reached. And, inasmuch as the deposits of customs receipts were
                    suspended primarily on account of financial difficulties consequent upon
                    European war and more recently because of loan negotiations, my Government
                    believes and earnestly recommends that your excellency’s Government should
                    forthwith resume the deposit of customs in accordance with the terms of the
                    existing contract.</p>
                <p>I avail [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chas. S. Hartman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
